# The transpiler rewrite's strict xfail list (TESTING.md, "Golden gate").
#
#   <input-set>/<relpath> <target> <reason>
#
# <target> is a dialect name, or `parse` (the output file's stem under the
# input's golden directory). The `ir` and `report` lines went with the IR
# (phase 6): `golden diff` passes over a baseline's `ir.json` and
# `report.json`. `golden diff --xfail` fails on
# any difference not listed here, and on a listed line that is now identical
# (XPASS): delete the line then. Every line is a reviewed, intended change.
#
# Baseline: baseline-1298f0b-fx17 (TESTING.md "Golden gate"), recorded from
# p7-integrate 1298f0b by team-lead's batch-7b gate (D47; batches 5, 6, 7
# landed on fx16). Every line this list held against baseline-9c7a7e0-fx16 was
# a reviewed, intended change and is now the baseline; the list starts empty.
# A new line goes under a section header naming its ledger row.

# S1: P4-017: a capacitor given by its charge is VACASK's source line `c1 (a b) i=ddt(q)` (docs/dev-builtin-behavioral.md
# at 36be560). Oracle: the ODE's closed form (tests/test_vacask_runs/devices.rs::p4_017_a_charge_capacitor_is_the_charges_ddt).
fixtures/tests/ltspice/p_charge_capacitor.cir vacask now written: a charge capacitor is the source line `i=ddt(q)` (P4-017)
ltspice/ltspice_examples/1677.net vacask now written: a charge capacitor is the source line `i=ddt(q)` (P4-017)
xyce/SOLN_DEP_CAP/voltDepCharge_test.cir vacask now written: a charge capacitor is the source line `i=ddt(q)` (P4-017)

